WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.420 --> 00:00:02.639
I'm kind of unpopular in the UFO

00:00:02.640 --> 00:00:04.139
community because a lot of people

00:00:04.140 --> 00:00:06.449
say that I'm a bit of a

00:00:06.450 --> 00:00:07.829
I'm a bit of a negative outlook and

00:00:07.830 --> 00:00:09.539
they prefer things to be aliens.

00:00:09.540 --> 00:00:11.459
All the UFO videos we

00:00:11.460 --> 00:00:13.409
have are blurry.

00:00:13.410 --> 00:00:14.799
And it's not because alien

00:00:14.800 --> 00:00:15.989
spaceships are blurry.

00:00:15.990 --> 00:00:17.639
It's because when you zoom in, you

00:00:17.640 --> 00:00:18.869
see that it's not an alien

00:00:18.870 --> 00:00:21.269
spaceship, at least so far.

00:00:21.270 --> 00:00:23.039
Science writer Mick West is the

00:00:23.040 --> 00:00:24.509
author of Escaping the Rabbit Hole

00:00:24.510 --> 00:00:26.159
How to Debunk Conspiracy Theories

00:00:26.160 --> 00:00:28.379
Using Facts, Logic, and Respect.

00:00:28.380 --> 00:00:29.789
And he runs a popular YouTube

00:00:29.790 --> 00:00:31.259
channel where he takes a detailed

00:00:31.260 --> 00:00:33.059
look at alleged UFO sightings,

00:00:33.060 --> 00:00:34.769
finding that phenomena thought to be

00:00:34.770 --> 00:00:36.449
visitors from another planet almost

00:00:36.450 --> 00:00:38.549
always have far more pedestrian

00:00:38.550 --> 00:00:39.599
explanations.

00:00:39.600 --> 00:00:41.399
It's almost like a spiral of lights

00:00:41.400 --> 00:00:43.529
rotating. It's very confusing.

00:00:43.530 --> 00:00:44.999
But several people on Reddit and

00:00:45.000 --> 00:00:46.859
Twitter have already suggested what

00:00:46.860 --> 00:00:48.689
I think is the correct explanation.

00:00:48.690 --> 00:00:50.699
Flares drop from three small

00:00:50.700 --> 00:00:52.289
planes. The only time I can't

00:00:52.290 --> 00:00:53.939
explain what a UFO is is when

00:00:53.940 --> 00:00:55.439
there's not enough information.

00:00:55.440 --> 00:00:57.569
On June 24th, 1947,

00:00:57.570 --> 00:00:59.129
a pilot named Kenneth Arnold saw

00:00:59.130 --> 00:01:01.109
nine disc shaped objects near

00:01:01.110 --> 00:01:02.759
Mt. Rainier, Washington, which was

00:01:02.760 --> 00:01:04.559
the first reported UFO sighting, and

00:01:04.560 --> 00:01:06.239
one factor in the decision to create

00:01:06.240 --> 00:01:07.829
Project Blue Book, a team of

00:01:07.830 --> 00:01:09.149
investigators with the U.S.

00:01:09.150 --> 00:01:11.129
Air Force that over 17 years studied

00:01:11.130 --> 00:01:12.779
the veracity of these claims.

00:01:12.780 --> 00:01:15.149
By the time it dissolved in 1969,

00:01:15.150 --> 00:01:17.519
the group had studied nearly 13,000

00:01:17.520 --> 00:01:19.379
UFO sightings, concluding that

00:01:19.380 --> 00:01:20.879
almost all of them could be

00:01:20.880 --> 00:01:22.499
attributed to other phenomena.

00:01:22.500 --> 00:01:25.139
5%, however, are still unexplained.

00:01:25.140 --> 00:01:26.579
The cultural obsession with flying

00:01:26.580 --> 00:01:28.409
saucers and alien invaders reflected

00:01:28.410 --> 00:01:29.729
Cold War fears of nuclear

00:01:29.730 --> 00:01:31.109
annihilation and communist

00:01:31.110 --> 00:01:32.279
infiltration.

00:01:32.280 --> 00:01:34.319
From the Blob to Close Encounters

00:01:34.320 --> 00:01:35.999
of the Third Kind to E.T.

00:01:36.000 --> 00:01:38.009
and The X-Files to Men in Black

00:01:38.010 --> 00:01:39.539
Hollywood stoked our fascination

00:01:39.540 --> 00:01:41.339
with the threat of foreign invasion.

00:01:41.340 --> 00:01:42.340
Mikey

00:01:43.320 --> 00:01:44.699
or the promise of connecting with

00:01:44.700 --> 00:01:46.529
visitors from another world.

00:01:46.530 --> 00:01:48.029
We're really looking for some kind

00:01:48.030 --> 00:01:50.159
of holy grail of UFO videos,

00:01:50.160 --> 00:01:51.239
which should be something that is

00:01:51.240 --> 00:01:53.369
unambiguously weird, something

00:01:53.370 --> 00:01:55.229
where we can look at this video and

00:01:55.230 --> 00:01:57.269
say, Oh, that's definitely something

00:01:57.270 --> 00:01:58.319
unusual.

00:01:58.320 --> 00:01:59.609
But that really hasn't come along

00:01:59.610 --> 00:02:01.529
yet. We're just seeing these fuzzy

00:02:01.530 --> 00:02:02.879
blobs in the distance.

00:02:02.880 --> 00:02:04.559
This video was leaked and it showed

00:02:04.560 --> 00:02:06.209
what looked like flying green

00:02:06.210 --> 00:02:07.139
triangles.

00:02:07.140 --> 00:02:09.089
It wasn't flying pyramids.

00:02:09.090 --> 00:02:10.288
It wasn't anything amazing.

00:02:10.289 --> 00:02:11.459
It wasn't UFOs.

00:02:11.460 --> 00:02:13.139
It was just a camera artifact caused

00:02:13.140 --> 00:02:14.219
by a triangular aperture.

00:02:14.220 --> 00:02:16.349
I think I've got a lens here and

00:02:16.350 --> 00:02:19.229
it has a triangular aperture.

00:02:19.230 --> 00:02:20.819
When you film things through it that

00:02:20.820 --> 00:02:22.469
are out of focus, it makes them into

00:02:22.470 --> 00:02:23.309
little triangles.

00:02:23.310 --> 00:02:25.139
In recent years, the UFO craze has

00:02:25.140 --> 00:02:26.849
migrated from the grocery store rag,

00:02:26.850 --> 00:02:28.229
the Weekly World to the New York

00:02:28.230 --> 00:02:30.179
Times, Time Magazine, Politico

00:02:30.180 --> 00:02:32.519
and Forbes in 2017,

00:02:32.520 --> 00:02:34.769
declassified video shot in 2004

00:02:34.770 --> 00:02:36.509
showed unusual radar readings off

00:02:36.510 --> 00:02:37.949
the coast of California that was

00:02:37.950 --> 00:02:38.939
captured by U.S.

00:02:38.940 --> 00:02:39.989
Navy pilots.

00:02:39.990 --> 00:02:42.059
It was covered on 60 Minutes.

00:02:42.060 --> 00:02:43.919
So as I'm coming down, it starts

00:02:43.920 --> 00:02:44.789
coming up.

00:02:44.790 --> 00:02:46.859
So it's mimicking your moves?

00:02:46.860 --> 00:02:48.329
Yeah, it was aware we were there.

00:02:48.330 --> 00:02:50.069
You'll see how close I get.

00:02:50.070 --> 00:02:51.689
So I go like this and it's climbing

00:02:51.690 --> 00:02:53.279
still, and it gets right in front of

00:02:53.280 --> 00:02:54.749
me. It just disappears.

00:02:54.750 --> 00:02:56.369
Disappear. Disappears.

00:02:56.370 --> 00:02:57.389
Like gone.

00:02:57.390 --> 00:02:59.279
West says that this video, now

00:02:59.280 --> 00:03:01.229
known as a Tic TAC UFO sighting, can

00:03:01.230 --> 00:03:02.519
easily be explained.

00:03:02.520 --> 00:03:04.109
If you actually analyze the video,

00:03:04.110 --> 00:03:05.879
you can go in and go frame by frame

00:03:05.880 --> 00:03:06.959
and look at what's actually

00:03:06.960 --> 00:03:08.909
happening. You see that every time

00:03:08.910 --> 00:03:10.349
the object moves.

00:03:10.350 --> 00:03:11.819
It's just because the camera is

00:03:11.820 --> 00:03:13.949
moving. Because every time you

00:03:13.950 --> 00:03:15.839
switch modes on the camera, he

00:03:15.840 --> 00:03:17.459
has to recapture the object, which

00:03:17.460 --> 00:03:19.499
means the object can keep moving off

00:03:19.500 --> 00:03:20.729
to the side. You can look at the

00:03:20.730 --> 00:03:22.259
numbers at the top of the screen and

00:03:22.260 --> 00:03:24.089
you see the camera is actually

00:03:24.090 --> 00:03:26.279
tracking from from right to left.

00:03:26.280 --> 00:03:27.539
And at the end of the video,

00:03:28.560 --> 00:03:30.059
all that's happened is it stops

00:03:30.060 --> 00:03:31.049
tracking.

00:03:31.050 --> 00:03:32.929
Now, if you're following an object,

00:03:32.930 --> 00:03:34.469
you're looking at, say, a race car

00:03:34.470 --> 00:03:36.299
through some binoculars and you

00:03:36.300 --> 00:03:38.279
stop rotating your head in

00:03:38.280 --> 00:03:39.869
the race track race car, which is

00:03:39.870 --> 00:03:41.369
like zip out of your field of

00:03:41.370 --> 00:03:41.939
vision.

00:03:41.940 --> 00:03:43.709
Mainstream buzz about UFOs reached a

00:03:43.710 --> 00:03:45.599
crescendo in 2017

00:03:45.600 --> 00:03:46.829
with a New York Times article

00:03:46.830 --> 00:03:48.989
headlined Glowing Auras and Black

00:03:48.990 --> 00:03:51.059
Money The Pentagon's Mysterious

00:03:51.060 --> 00:03:52.109
UFO Program.

00:03:52.110 --> 00:03:53.459
It revealed that the Pentagon had

00:03:53.460 --> 00:03:55.299
secretly secured $22

00:03:55.300 --> 00:03:58.139
million to investigate the subject.

00:03:58.140 --> 00:03:59.609
That was one of the biggest stories,

00:03:59.610 --> 00:04:01.769
if not the biggest story

00:04:01.770 --> 00:04:03.569
that the New York Times digital

00:04:03.570 --> 00:04:05.649
edition ever had.

00:04:05.650 --> 00:04:06.650
Sky.

00:04:08.270 --> 00:04:09.919
It sounds like a plot out of The

00:04:09.920 --> 00:04:11.779
X-Files, part of a once

00:04:11.780 --> 00:04:13.879
secret government program

00:04:13.880 --> 00:04:15.769
to investigate sightings of

00:04:15.770 --> 00:04:17.659
so-called anomalous aerial

00:04:17.660 --> 00:04:19.159
vehicles in the skies.

00:04:19.160 --> 00:04:20.479
The entire government, what they

00:04:20.480 --> 00:04:22.369
were doing, they kind

00:04:22.370 --> 00:04:24.859
of disguised the program as

00:04:24.860 --> 00:04:26.959
if it was just about the future

00:04:26.960 --> 00:04:28.039
of aerospace.

00:04:28.040 --> 00:04:29.479
And they phrased it as saying, you

00:04:29.480 --> 00:04:31.069
know, we are going to study what

00:04:31.070 --> 00:04:32.839
needs to happen in aerospace over

00:04:32.840 --> 00:04:34.189
the next 20 years.

00:04:34.190 --> 00:04:36.259
And then we had these videos, which

00:04:36.260 --> 00:04:38.299
actually came from the US government

00:04:38.300 --> 00:04:39.649
that appeared to show things that

00:04:39.650 --> 00:04:41.149
were really, really interesting.

00:04:41.150 --> 00:04:42.619
So that got everybody kind of

00:04:42.620 --> 00:04:44.179
talking about it and thinking that

00:04:44.180 --> 00:04:46.369
there was something to the story.

00:04:46.370 --> 00:04:48.229
Do you think the government knows

00:04:48.230 --> 00:04:50.119
more about UFOs or UAPs than

00:04:50.120 --> 00:04:51.979
they're letting on?

00:04:51.980 --> 00:04:52.759
You know, the government is this

00:04:52.760 --> 00:04:53.830
big, you

00:04:54.950 --> 00:04:56.809
know, very difficult to get to

00:04:56.810 --> 00:04:58.129
grips with, very complicated

00:04:58.130 --> 00:04:59.479
organization with lots of moving

00:04:59.480 --> 00:05:00.769
parts that they don't talk to each

00:05:00.770 --> 00:05:02.569
other. So there are these weird

00:05:02.570 --> 00:05:04.789
little corners of it here and there.

00:05:04.790 --> 00:05:06.679
And it's not like the entire

00:05:06.680 --> 00:05:08.029
Pentagon that's been studying

00:05:08.030 --> 00:05:09.259
crashed UFOs.

00:05:09.260 --> 00:05:11.059
There's a large body of secrets that

00:05:11.060 --> 00:05:12.889
the government has, and partly

00:05:12.890 --> 00:05:14.479
this is out of necessity.

00:05:14.480 --> 00:05:16.699
There are obvious national security

00:05:16.700 --> 00:05:18.589
implications, but also a large part

00:05:18.590 --> 00:05:20.119
of it is just the default position

00:05:20.120 --> 00:05:21.259
of the government. There's an

00:05:21.260 --> 00:05:23.299
excessive amount of secrecy, which

00:05:23.300 --> 00:05:25.309
is is a bureaucratic

00:05:25.310 --> 00:05:26.149
burden.

00:05:26.150 --> 00:05:27.739
It would be great if they would tell

00:05:27.740 --> 00:05:29.749
us more about what they know, about

00:05:29.750 --> 00:05:31.729
what these videos are, what

00:05:31.730 --> 00:05:33.289
analysis they have done.

00:05:33.290 --> 00:05:34.819
There are very real issues that you

00:05:34.820 --> 00:05:36.649
could say fall under the rubric of

00:05:36.650 --> 00:05:38.119
UFOs or UAPs.

00:05:38.120 --> 00:05:39.949
If a pilot sees an object

00:05:39.950 --> 00:05:41.899
in the sky and they can't identify

00:05:41.900 --> 00:05:43.519
what that object is, we can't just

00:05:43.520 --> 00:05:44.959
ignore that. We can't just pretend

00:05:44.960 --> 00:05:46.069
it didn't happen.

00:05:46.070 --> 00:05:47.179
And we know this type of thing

00:05:47.180 --> 00:05:48.709
happens a lot because pilots give

00:05:48.710 --> 00:05:49.849
these reports.

00:05:49.850 --> 00:05:51.619
So in that sense, we need to figure

00:05:51.620 --> 00:05:52.609
out what's going on.

00:05:52.610 --> 00:05:54.019
The New York Times bombshell led to

00:05:54.020 --> 00:05:55.429
a frenzy of new interest.

00:05:55.430 --> 00:05:57.259
In 2020, the Pentagon established

00:05:57.260 --> 00:05:59.119
a task force to study UAPs or

00:05:59.120 --> 00:06:00.799
unidentified aerial phenomena.

00:06:00.800 --> 00:06:02.329
And just a year later, with a push

00:06:02.330 --> 00:06:04.279
from Senator Marco Rubio, Congress

00:06:04.280 --> 00:06:05.689
demanded that the task force release

00:06:05.690 --> 00:06:07.159
a report on everything it knows

00:06:07.160 --> 00:06:08.659
about UFO sightings.

00:06:08.660 --> 00:06:10.519
That report ran just nine

00:06:10.520 --> 00:06:11.359
pages.

00:06:11.360 --> 00:06:12.859
What's happening in government now

00:06:12.860 --> 00:06:14.149
is they're trying to get past some

00:06:14.150 --> 00:06:16.579
kind of whistleblower protection.

00:06:16.580 --> 00:06:17.599
They're trying to make it so that

00:06:17.600 --> 00:06:19.489
people can come forward and tell

00:06:19.490 --> 00:06:21.379
their stories of having seen some

00:06:21.380 --> 00:06:23.599
kind of UFO without worrying

00:06:23.600 --> 00:06:25.249
about non-disclosure agreements.

00:06:25.250 --> 00:06:27.019
UAP focused startups are popping up

00:06:27.020 --> 00:06:28.669
everywhere with a focus on building

00:06:28.670 --> 00:06:29.899
better detection equipment and

00:06:29.900 --> 00:06:30.709
software.

00:06:30.710 --> 00:06:32.299
Seemingly, their goal is to contend

00:06:32.300 --> 00:06:33.799
for military contracts if the

00:06:33.800 --> 00:06:35.209
government continues allocating

00:06:35.210 --> 00:06:36.889
funding to study the issue.

00:06:36.890 --> 00:06:38.749
The big rumor that is getting

00:06:38.750 --> 00:06:39.979
everyone excited in the UFO

00:06:39.980 --> 00:06:41.629
community right now is the US

00:06:41.630 --> 00:06:43.759
government actually has

00:06:43.760 --> 00:06:46.009
recovered some kind of material

00:06:46.010 --> 00:06:47.929
or technology from crashed

00:06:47.930 --> 00:06:49.189
flying saucers.

00:06:49.190 --> 00:06:50.389
They think there's a crashed

00:06:50.390 --> 00:06:52.399
retrieval program within

00:06:52.400 --> 00:06:53.599
the US government.

00:06:53.600 --> 00:06:55.309
At a congressional hearing, Deputy

00:06:55.310 --> 00:06:57.079
Director of Navy Intelligence Scott

00:06:57.080 --> 00:06:59.179
Bray said this wasn't true.

00:06:59.180 --> 00:07:01.819
Have we come across any wreckage

00:07:01.820 --> 00:07:02.989
of any kind of

00:07:04.340 --> 00:07:06.319
object that

00:07:06.320 --> 00:07:08.389
has now been examined by you?

00:07:09.800 --> 00:07:11.119
The UAP task force doesn't have any

00:07:11.120 --> 00:07:13.819
wreckage that isn't explainable,

00:07:13.820 --> 00:07:15.139
that isn't consistent with being of

00:07:15.140 --> 00:07:16.429
terrestrial origin.

00:07:16.430 --> 00:07:17.539
We might get somebody in the

00:07:17.540 --> 00:07:18.979
government who says that they were

00:07:18.980 --> 00:07:20.809
tasked at some time

00:07:20.810 --> 00:07:22.669
to investigate a mysterious piece

00:07:22.670 --> 00:07:24.709
of metal or that somebody

00:07:24.710 --> 00:07:26.629
in the government thought that this

00:07:26.630 --> 00:07:28.339
particular piece of metal came from

00:07:28.340 --> 00:07:30.169
a crashed flying saucer.

00:07:30.170 --> 00:07:31.339
But that wouldn't be surprising to

00:07:31.340 --> 00:07:31.819
me.

00:07:31.820 --> 00:07:33.289
If there's something unusual in our

00:07:33.290 --> 00:07:34.849
airspace, it certainly warrants

00:07:34.850 --> 00:07:35.749
careful study.

00:07:35.750 --> 00:07:37.639
But for now, at least, whatever

00:07:37.640 --> 00:07:38.929
is out there is far more likely to

00:07:38.930 --> 00:07:40.729
be a flare of light, a balloon or

00:07:40.730 --> 00:07:42.589
even a plane than visitors from

00:07:42.590 --> 00:07:43.939
a faraway planet.

00:07:43.940 --> 00:07:46.189
If there's evidence of

00:07:46.190 --> 00:07:48.019
new technology flying around in the

00:07:48.020 --> 00:07:50.029
skies, anti-gravity, that's worth

00:07:50.030 --> 00:07:52.429
billions and billions of dollars.

00:07:52.430 --> 00:07:54.319
And we should spend billions

00:07:54.320 --> 00:07:55.969
of dollars investigating it.

00:07:55.970 --> 00:07:57.649
But we don't. And I think the reason

00:07:57.650 --> 00:07:59.209
we don't is that the evidence really

00:07:59.210 --> 00:08:00.139
isn't there.

00:08:00.140 --> 00:08:01.309
The government knows more about

00:08:01.310 --> 00:08:02.539
everything that it's willing to tell

00:08:02.540 --> 00:08:04.159
us. It's dubious that it knows

00:08:04.160 --> 00:08:06.349
anything about UFOs being aliens,

00:08:06.350 --> 00:08:07.350
though.

